SUMMARY:WAVES VIENNA: AGATHA IS DEAD (DE) / GROßKIND (AT) / TURBO TRANS TURISTI (RS) / SLOE NOON (DE) (Uhrzeit prüfen)
LOCATION:Chelsea
DESCRIPTION:Doors: 18:15   SLOE NOON (DE) – 18:30 Sloe Noon is the project of guitarist and vocalist Anna Olivia Böke\, drawing inspiration from both countries she has called home. Blending the in?uences of British alternative rock with the krautrock rhythms of Germany’s Ruhr region\, Sloe Noon creates a distinctive mix of guitar-driven pop\, alt-rock and shoegaze. Joined on stage by live drums\, guitar and bass\, her performances invite audiences into the dreamy bedroom where the songs were written – only to tear down its walls together. https://linktr.ee/sloenoon    TURBO TRANS TURISTI (RS) – 19:45 Turbo Trans Turisti is an alternative pop band from Belgrade\, founded by two brothers\, Nikola and Boško Mijuškovi?. The band was formed in 2017 in a family bedroom that also served as a studio\, where their Wirst two albums\, Levo ili Desno (2018) and Ništa Nije Strašno (2024)\, were recorded. Albums have been released for Pop Depresija\, and one live album\, Šta bre? Kontrolisani Haos! Kome Treba Kontrola? (2024)\, for the same music label. TTT have performed at numerous showcase festivals throughout their career\, including MENT\, Tallinn Music Week\, Poland Music Week\, MMB\, ESNS\, as well as music festivals such as Belgrade Beer Fest\, Arsenal Fest\, Tam Tam\, and others. Their concerts are known for their raw\, honest emotion and high-energy performances\, delivered with almost no pauses throughout the set. The band consists of three members: Boško on guitar and vocals\, Nikola on samplers\, synth\, and vocals\, and Andrej on drums. www.instagram.com/ttturisti/?hl=de    GROßKIND (AT) – 21:00 GroßKind are not heroes. The four-piece band creates indie (?st-in-your-face) pop\, balancing emotional piano ballads with raw punk in?uences. Their songs confront uncomfortable truths while leaving space to let go\, sing along\, and simply be yourself. Shaped by deep friendship\, uncompromising honesty\, and mutual trust\, GroßKind's sound feels like hot summer days in a grey city. Their debut single\, "Keine Helden"\, released in June 2026\, offers a ?rst taste of the band's energetic live shows – featuring lyrics that hit like a slap in the face and music that feels like a cool\, soft pillow on a summer day. Following a memorable secret hometown show\, demand for the band's ?rst Vienna release concert was so high that it sold out within two hours and had to be moved to a larger venue. GroßKind are currently working on new releases while continuing to shape their unmistakably honest sound through a collaborative and organic creative process. www.instagram.com/grosskind.band/    AGATHA IS DEAD (DE) – 22:15 Formed in the lockdown winter of 2021\, Agatha Is Dead! began as a post-punk experiment between longtime friends Lilly and Noah\, who ?rst made music together in their school days. Their shared love for Joy Division\, The Cure\, Molchat Doma\, and Fontaines D.C. laid the foundation for their darkly urgent sound. With the addition of drummer Joey Ramone Hansen−bringing grunge and pop−punk bite−and Arthur on bass\, the band played their ?rst shows in 2022 and quickly carved out a place in Berlin's underground scene. www.instagram.com/agathaisdeadband/?hl=de  www.wavesvienna.com/  Tickets: www.universe.com/events/waves-vienna-2026-tickets-3KLWXG
